      "created_at": "2026-09-15T21:12:05Z",
      "updated_at": "2026-09-15T21:12:05Z",
      "body": "I looked into this and the throw does not originate in this repository — it comes from the `@openfoodfacts/openfoodfacts-webcomponents` dependency, in `web-components/src/localization/index.ts`:\n\n```ts\nexport const setLanguageCode = (newLanguageCode: string) => {\n  if (!(targetLocales as readonly string[]).includes(newLanguageCode)) {\n    throw new Error(`Invalid language code: ${newLanguageCode}`)\n  }\n  setLocale(newLanguageCode)\n  languageCode.set(newLanguageCode)\n}\n```\n\n`targetLocales` comes from the Lit Localize config, which currently lists **111 locales** — the ones that have a compiled translation bundle. `en` is included; `ab` is not.\n\nSo as @hangy noted, `ab` is a perfectly valid ISO 639-1 code that ProductOpener supports — it just has no translation yet. The result is that a *valid but untranslated* language throws instead of degrading. Since `setLanguageCode` is reached from `attributeChangedCallback`, the exception breaks the component rather than falling back.\n\nThis is not specific to Abkhaz: it affects every language Open Food Facts supports that Crowdin has not produced a bundle for yet, which in practice means minority languages are the ones that break.\n\n**Proposed fix:** in `setLanguageCode`, fall back to `sourceLocale` and emit a `console.warn` instead of throwing, so an untranslated language renders in English rather than crashing the component.\n\nTwo questions before I open a PR in `openfoodfacts-webcomponents`:\n\n1. Do you prefer the graceful fallback above, or would you rather add the missing codes to `targetLocales`? The fallback seems more robust to me, since the Crowdin-driven list will always lag behind the set of languages the database accepts — but it is your call.\n2. Should the fallback be silent, or is a `console.warn` acceptable in production?\n\nHappy to implement whichever you prefer.\n\n@Naivedhyajain20 — you asked about this back in June; if you are still working on it I am glad to step aside, otherwise I will pick it up.\n\n---\n\n*Disclosure per `AGENTS.md`: I am using Claude Code (model: Opus 5) agentically to assist with this investigation. The diagnosis above was verified against the current sources on `main`.*\n",
